# Reference crontab for the Geyam VPS (Phase 6).
#
# Install (as root):
#   crontab -e
# then paste these lines, leaving the existing PATH / SHELL declarations alone.
# Verify with: crontab -l
#
# All scripts are idempotent; multiple runs are harmless. Each pings its own
# Healthchecks.io URL (sourced from /etc/default/geyam) so red-on-the-dashboard
# means that specific job didn't complete.

# Daily DB backup → R2 (Phase 3).
0 2 * * * /opt/geyam/ops/backup.sh

# Monthly restore drill (Phase 3 step 7 + Phase 6 step 2). First Sunday of the
# month at 03:00 — picked to follow backup, but well before peak hours.
0 3 1-7 * 0 /opt/geyam/ops/restore-drill.sh

# Hourly api healthz heartbeat (Phase 6 step 2). Offset 5 min so backup at 02:00
# isn't tripped over by a probe.
5 * * * * /opt/geyam/ops/heartbeat-api.sh

# Hourly chenki HF Space wakeup (Phase 6 step 2). Offset 15 min so api + chenki
# probes are staggered.
15 * * * * /opt/geyam/ops/heartbeat-chenki.sh

# Daily past-due → suspended sweeper (Phase 9 step 9). Runs at 04:00; flips
# subscriptions whose past_due_since exceeds the 7-day grace period.
0 4 * * * docker exec geyam-backend-1 python -m scripts.sweep_past_due
